From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The follower through doors and stairs with the player (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The follower went into its ball whenever the player went through a door,
up or down stairs or into a cave or a forest (the game walks the player
in: "the game moves the player"), and came out again only once the
player stood still, its ball first. Now it goes with them, as
HeartGold's does: during a warp's way in or out (the task sub_02056BDC
and sub_02056C18 start: FieldSystem_PortInWarp) it isn't put away, and
on the other side it's out at once without its ball, behind the player
or, on their tile (a door's, the stairs'), shown once they've stepped
off it. And when it is in its ball and the player sets off walking, it
comes out behind them as they go, growing out of nothing, instead of
waiting for them to stop (its ball, as before, when they stand).
---
  include/unk_02056B30.h |  4 +++
  src/port_follower.c    | 71 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
  src/unk_02056B30.c     | 18 +++++++++++++
  3 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

